    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-white mb-4">3,117 Lawsuits and Counting: Is Your Website Next?</h1>
    <p class="text-gray-400 mb-8">Published July 4, 2026</p>

    <p class="text-lg text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
      Federal ADA Title III website accessibility lawsuits hit <strong>3,117 in 2025</strong> — a 27% jump from the year before. That is not a typo. Over 3,000 businesses, most with fewer than 50 employees, were served with federal lawsuits because their websites were not accessible.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mt-10 mb-4">The Numbers Do Not Lie</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
      Here is what the data shows:
    </p>
    <ul class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
      <li><strong>3,117 federal ADA website lawsuits</strong> filed in 2025</li>
      <li><strong>27% increase</strong> year-over-year</li>
      <li><strong>73% of defendants</strong> had fewer than 50 employees</li>
      <li><strong>California alone:</strong> 478 lawsuits per month, driven by the Unruh Civil Rights Act ($4,000 per violation)</li>
      <li><strong>Illinois surged 745%</strong> as plaintiff firms relocated from New York</li>
      <li><strong>Shopify stores</strong> represented 32% of all web accessibility lawsuits</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mt-10 mb-4">Who Is Being Targeted?</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
      This is not just happening to big corporations. <strong>Small businesses are the #1 target.</strong> Plumbers, dentists, restaurants, HVAC companies, retail shops — any business with a website that the public can visit is exposed.
    </p>
    <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
      In California, the Unruh Civil Rights Act adds a statutory minimum of <strong>$4,000 per violation</strong> on top of federal ADA claims. A single lawsuit can cost $10,000–$50,000+ in legal fees and settlement costs.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mt-10 mb-4">The "Accessibility Widget" Trap</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
      Here is a hard truth: <strong>26% of businesses that were sued had an accessibility widget installed.</strong> Overlay widgets like AccessiBe, UserWay, and AudioEye do not make your site compliant. Courts have repeatedly ruled that widgets are not a substitute for real WCAG compliance.
    </p>
    <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
      In fact, the National Federation of the Blind and over 400 accessibility advocates have signed a statement saying overlay widgets should not be used. Installing one can actually <em>increase</em> your legal risk by signaling you knew about accessibility issues but chose a band-aid instead of a real fix.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mt-10 mb-4">What Actually Protects You</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
      Real compliance means:
    </p>
    <ul class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
      <li>WCAG 2.2 AA conformance — the standard courts measure against</li>
      <li>Proper alt text on all images</li>
      <li>Keyboard navigation that works</li>
      <li>Sufficient color contrast ratios</li>
      <li>Missing legal pages: Privacy Policy, Terms of Service, Accessibility Statement, DMCA Notice</li>
      <li>Regular audits — compliance is not one-and-done</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mt-10 mb-4">The 4 Pages Most Businesses Are Missing</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
      Across 100% of the businesses we scanned, the same four pages were missing:
    </p>
    <ol class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2">
      <li><strong>Privacy Policy</strong> — Required by CCPA and expected in ADA lawsuits</li>
      <li><strong>Terms of Service</strong> — Establishes your legal boundaries</li>
      <li><strong>Accessibility Statement</strong> — Shows good-faith effort toward compliance</li>
      <li><strong>DMCA Notice</strong> — Required if anyone can upload content to your site</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
      These four pages are the fastest, cheapest compliance wins you can get. We include them in every compliance package.
    </p>

